// `std::math` (spec/21 §3d, `rule.arith.float-fns`): `sqrt`, `floor`,
// `ceil`, `round`, `trunc`, `ln`, `exp`, `log2`, `log10`, `sin`, `cos`,
// `tan`, `atan2` and `powf`. Each takes an `f32` or `f64` (`atan2` and
// `powf` two of one type) and gives that type, which no bound can say,
// so both implementations realize them natively, and none is written
// here.
